# Numeric input (no letters)

Fields that only accept numbers must never keep letters or other junk from typing/paste — even when `keyboardType` is `decimal-pad` / `number-pad` (external keyboards and paste still allow text).

## Required

1. Sanitize with `@/utils/parse`:
   - `sanitizeNumericInput(text)` — decimals (default; allows `,` thousands + one `.`)
   - `sanitizeNumericInput(text, { decimals: false })` — integers only
   - `numericOnChangeText(onChangeText, options?)` — wrap handlers for raw `TextInput`s
2. Prefer the shared `Input` primitive — it auto-sanitizes when `keyboardType` is `decimal-pad`, `number-pad`, or `numeric`.
3. Raw `TextInput`s with those keyboard types **must** use `numericOnChangeText` (or call `sanitizeNumericInput` before setState).

## Do / Don't

```tsx
// ✅ Input auto-sanitizes
<Input keyboardType="decimal-pad" value={amount} onChangeText={setAmount} />

// ✅ Raw TextInput
<TextInput
  keyboardType="decimal-pad"
  value={rateText}
  onChangeText={numericOnChangeText(onRateChange)}
/>

// ❌ Letters can leak in
<TextInput keyboardType="decimal-pad" value={rate} onChangeText={setRate} />
```

## Never reintroduce

- Ad-hoc `/[^0-9]/g` (or similar) copies when `sanitizeNumericInput` fits
- Number fields that set state from unsanitized `onChangeText` text
